>> title: Ham and Macaroni Soup
>> category: Soups
>> tags: macaroni, ham, eggs, hong kong, breakfast, quick
>> counters: Cha Chaan Teng
>> aka: fo teui tung fan, tong tung fan, 火腿通粉, 湯通粉, 餐肉通粉, ham and macaroni soup, ham macaroni soup, macaroni in soup, macaroni soup
>> pairs-with: chicken-broth
>> servings: 2
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: narrow — the macaroni is boiled in its own water for a reason: cooked in the broth it sheds starch and the bowl comes out cloudy and thick
>> step.1: boil 8 min in its own water, drain
>> step.2: warm the broth with the ham, 5 min
>> step.3: fry the eggs 3 min, whites set and yolks loose
>> step.4: ladle the broth over the macaroni, egg alongside

Boil @elbow macaroni{4%oz}(115 g) in a #saucepan{} of salted water for ~boil{8%min}, then drain it.

Warm @chicken stock{3%cups}(700 mL) with @sliced ham{3%oz}(85 g; cut in ribbons), @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} and @white pepper{1/4%tsp} for ~simmer{5%min}.

Fry @eggs{2%large} in @neutral oil{1%Tbs} in a #frying pan{} for ~fry{3%min}, until the whites are set and the yolks are still loose.

Ladle @&(~2)ham broth{} over @&(~3)macaroni{} in two deep bowls, slide @&(~1)fried egg{} alongside rather than in, and scatter @scallion{1}(thinly sliced) over.
